  "threshold_reasoning": "In job fraud screening, false negatives (failing to identify scams) expose vulnerable job seekers to financial fraud, advance fee scams, and identity theft. Conversely, false positives (flagging legitimate listings) trigger manual review or entity verification steps. We prioritize high recall (>=75%) while preserving strong precision. Balanced Logistic Regression at threshold 0.65 yields 80.83% precision and 78.86% recall on the holdout test set (F1=0.7984). Standard Logistic Regression at threshold 0.10 achieves 80.49% recall, 55.62% precision, with superior empirical probability calibration (Brier score 0.0228, ECE 0.0293)."
